== Bugs ==
{{Bug|If you activate and resume "Pause" while an enemy emits projectiles, the bullets won't proceed with regular but instead extremely decreased speed. However, they will still pass intended range, which bypasses the effect of shot speed being reduced as it normally would with any items that slow projectiles down.}}
{{Bug|When used with {{i|Dad's Ring}}/{{i|Monstrance}}/{{i|Saturnus}} it creates a second ring/aura/circle of light that stays in place where Isaac used "Pause" which lasts for the active item's duration. The second ring/aura/circle is a visual glitch and does not interact with enemies. Moreover, both rings/auras/circles are flashing for the duration. When used while {{i|Telekinesis}} is active Pause creates a second ring that stays in place where Isaac used "Pause" which lasts for Telekinesis's remaining duration. Moreover both rings are flashing and the second ring can not block enemy tears for the duration. Any tears that were still caught in Telekinesis’s radius before using Pause become incredibly slowed and indefinitely follow Isaac until he shoots. The items {{i|Salvation}}, {{i|Spear Of Destiny}}, and {{i|Trinity Shield}} all have a similar bug however these items are completely unable to interact with enemies (or block enemy tears for the shield) while Pause is activated.}}
{{Bug|dlc=r|When used with {{i|Star of Bethlehem}} the light aura will be stuck in the last position before Pause was used even if the familiar continues without it. This is only a visual glitch, Isaac still has to be near the star to receive its benefits. If Pause’s effect ends the light instantly disappears and respawns back around the star again. The light will still fade when the star leaves the room.}}
{{Bug|dlc=r|When used with {{i|Dark Arts}}, the player can unintentionally Soft-lock themselves if the Pause item is used during the effects of Dark Arts, this can be fixed by quitting then entering the game again. This is because Dark Arts does not finish its animation due to the pause item locking it in place. In addition to this, the player cannot escape this soft-lock via the fire button due to the player not being able to fire during the effects of Dark Arts. Moreover if this bug happens while {{c|Tainted Judas}} has {{I|Birthright}}, the dark aura around Tainted Judas will experience a visual bug from Pause that is similar to {{i|Monstrance}}.}}

